\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is deciding whether a finite nonempty simple uncolored graph has WL identifying dimension at most a binary integer k EXPTIME-complete under deterministic polynomial-time many-one reductions, using ordinary color refinement in dimension one and joint tuple refinement at higher dimensions?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is deciding whether a finite nonempty simple uncolored graph has WL identifying dimension at most a binary integer k EXPTIME-complete under deterministic polynomial-time many-one reductions, using ordinary color refinement in dimension one and joint tuple refinement at higher dimensions?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-complexity-of-identifying-a-graph-by-Weisfeiler-Leman-refinement-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

